      ],
      "source": "https://www.cochisecountyhistoricalsociety.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bisbee serves as the county seat, while Sierra Vista is the most populous city in Cochise County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cochise_County%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cochise County includes the Sierra Vista‑Douglas metropolitan statistical area, linking two key regional hubs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cochise_County%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The county borders southwestern New Mexico and the northwestern Mexican state of Sonora, placing it at a tri‑border crossroads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
